  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only multiprofile avgpool with PCA is the strongest result so far (accuracy 0.591, F1 0.573), while image-only single ResNet50 is weak (accuracy 0.208). The key uncertainty is whether the image modality can become useful under the same multiprofile avgpool setting that helped RNA, before adding fusion complexity. config_011 tests image-only ResNet50 with multiprofile avgpool, directly extending the weak image-only baseline and mirroring the successful RNA profile/aggregation choice without changing the encoder or introducing fusion. This is the best next use of budget because it reduces uncertainty about image utility and helps decide whether multimodal ResNet50 fusion experiments are worth testing next."
